***************************************************************************************************************************************
Configuring Data Guard Broker
***************************************************************************************************************************************

1. Enable Flashback Database in Primary and Standby Databases
Enabling Flashback Database ensures that Data Guard Broker can manage failovers and reinstates efficiently, reducing downtime and administrative effort.
#Primary

SQL> ALTER DATABASE FLASHBACK ON

Database altered.

#Standby
SQL> ALTER DATABASE FLASHBACK ON;

Database altered.

2. Creating Data Guard Broker Configuraiton Files and Enabling them in Primary and Standby Databases.

#Primary
SQL> ALTER SYSTEM SET DG_BROKER_CONFIG_FILE1='+DATA/PRIMCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/dgb_config01.ora' SCOPE=BOTH;

System altered.
SQL> ALTER SYSTEM SET DG_BROKER_CONFIG_FILE2='+FRA/PRIMCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/dgb_config02.ora' SCOPE=BOTH;

System altered.

#Verify the Data Guard Broker Configuraiton Files
SQL> show parameter DG_BROKER

NAME                                 TYPE        VALUE
------------------------------------ ----------- ------------------------------
dg_broker_config_file1               string      +DATA/PRIMCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/d
                                                 gb_config01.ora
dg_broker_config_file2               string      +FRA/PRIMCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/dg
                                                 b_config02.ora
dg_broker_start                      boolean     FALSE


SQL> ALTER SYSTEM SET DG_BROKER_START=TRUE SCOPE=BOTH; 

System altered.

SQL> show parameter DG_BROKER

NAME                                 TYPE        VALUE
------------------------------------ ----------- ------------------------------
dg_broker_config_file1               string      +DATA/PRIMCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/d
                                                 gb_config01.ora
dg_broker_config_file2               string      +FRA/PRIMCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/dg
                                                 b_config02.ora
dg_broker_start                      boolean     TRUE


#Standby
SQL> ALTER SYSTEM SET DG_BROKER_CONFIG_FILE1='+DATA/STDBYCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/dgb_config01.ora' SCOPE=BOTH;

System altered.

SQL> ALTER SYSTEM SET DG_BROKER_CONFIG_FILE2='+FRA/STDBYCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/dgb_config02.ora' SCOPE=BOTH;

System altered.

#Verify the Data Guard Broker Configuraiton Files

SQL> show parameter DG_BROKER

NAME                                 TYPE        VALUE
------------------------------------ ----------- ------------------------------
dg_broker_config_file1               string      +DATA/STDBYCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/
                                                 dgb_config01.ora
dg_broker_config_file2               string      +FRA/STDBYCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/d
                                                 gb_config02.ora
dg_broker_start                      boolean     FALSE

SQL> ALTER SYSTEM SET DG_BROKER_START=TRUE SCOPE=BOTH; 

System altered.

3. Reset LOG_ARCHIVE_DEST_2 on Standby only
 On the standby to remove any manual redo transport configuration, allowing Data Guard Broker to fully control and correctly configure redo transport without conflicts.

SQL> ALTER SYSTEM RESET LOG_ARCHIVE_DEST_2 SCOPE=BOTH;

System altered.

SQL> show parameter DG_BROKER

NAME                                 TYPE        VALUE
------------------------------------ ----------- ------------------------------
dg_broker_config_file1               string      +DATA/STDBYCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/
                                                 dgb_config01.ora
dg_broker_config_file2               string      +FRA/STDBYCA/DATAGUARDCONFIG/d
                                                 gb_config02.ora
dg_broker_start                      boolean     TRUE


4. Creating Data Guard Broker Configuration

[oracle@caoraobs admin]$ dgmgrl sys/**********@PRIMCA as sysdba
